PATCH 2 — Fix the anime.js v4 default-import crash in src/App.jsx
Your bundle is anime.js v4 (no default export). `import anime from 'animejs'`
is undefined -> "anime is not a function" on every route.

- import anime from 'animejs';
+ import { animate, stagger } from 'animejs';

Replace the mount effect:
  useEffect(() => {
    if (window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) return;
    const anim = animate('.eyebrow', {
      opacity: [0, 1], translateY: [-20, 0],
      duration: 600, delay: stagger(50), ease: 'outQuad',
    });
    return () => anim && anim.revert && anim.revert();
  }, []);

Also: delete the stray 'use client' (Vite SPA), and delete any committed
src/.../anime.min.js (duplicates the npm package).
